WEBVTT

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:08.779
<v Sarah Okafor>Morning, everyone. You all there? Before we start — the football last night. Honestly, what was that?</v>

00:00:09.859 --> 00:00:12.660
<v Marcus Hale>Depends which bit of it you slept through.</v>

00:00:13.009 --> 00:00:14.410
<v Sarah Okafor>Unfortunately, none of it.</v>

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:18.519
<v Callum Reid>That explains the cheerful Monday face, then.</v>

00:00:18.949 --> 00:00:22.100
<v Sarah Okafor>Cheeky. It's Teams, that's just what the camera does.</v>

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:30.640
<v Marcus Hale>I was making weekend plans instead. Thought we'd get out for a walk next weekend, but the weather forecast's already looking miserable.</v>

00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:35.109
<v Jamie Brennan>It's Monday, Marcus. It'll have changed about eight times by then.</v>

00:00:36.219 --> 00:00:39.020
<v Marcus Hale>Yeah, and seven of those will be rain.</v>

00:00:40.969 --> 00:00:44.820
<v Fiona Doyle>Sorry, am I coming through? My headset did that thing again.</v>

00:00:46.090 --> 00:00:52.039
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah, got you, Fiona. Right, Monday the eighteenth. Let's separate what's finished from what actually needs doing.</v>

00:00:52.829 --> 00:00:59.829
<v Callum Reid>Yeah so, I signed off the inspection on the AC1 on Tuesday. That's finished, not something hanging over for today.</v>

00:01:02.189 --> 00:01:03.390
<v David Whitfield>Last Tuesday, yeah?</v>

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:09.810
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, last Tuesday. Just closing the loop, not volunteering to inspect it twice.</v>

00:01:11.120 --> 00:01:16.370
<v Sarah Okafor>And I already swapped the filter on the IM2 yesterday. That one's done as well.</v>

00:01:18.349 --> 00:01:21.849
<v Aisha Begum>Right, so the IM2 filter isn't part of today's list.</v>

00:01:23.049 --> 00:01:24.250
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly.</v>

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:30.349
<v Fiona Doyle>I finished the repair on the boiler last night, too. That's complete.</v>

00:01:32.390 --> 00:01:41.140
<v David Whitfield>Just so we don't mix the two up — I'm still waiting on parts for the big boiler. Nothing we can do until they arrive.</v>

00:01:43.540 --> 00:01:47.040
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, different one. I'm not saying the big boiler's repaired.</v>

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:52.629
<v Sarah Okafor>Understood. Big boiler stays blocked, no new action against it today.</v>

00:01:53.359 --> 00:02:03.159
<v David Whitfield>While I'm on, I noticed the stretch wrapper was running a bit warm on nights, but it settled down. Just an observation, not asking for work on it.</v>

00:02:05.209 --> 00:02:07.310
<v Aisha Begum>Settled back down on its own?</v>

00:02:07.959 --> 00:02:09.710
<v David Whitfield>Yeah. Nothing outstanding from that.</v>

00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:21.539
<v Sarah Okafor>Right. Fiona, can you sort the permit to work and isolation for the Injection Moulding Line 1 today? That's holding production up so it needs doing first.</v>

00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:29.099
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the Injection Moulding Line 1 today. First priority.</v>

00:02:30.050 --> 00:02:34.599
<v Callum Reid>That's the important bit for us. Not just having the paperwork sat there.</v>

00:02:36.580 --> 00:02:40.780
<v Fiona Doyle>No, understood — the permit and isolation, both. That's what I'm taking.</v>

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:48.039
<v Sarah Okafor>Good. David Whitfield, can you send the shift handover report round this morning, whenever you get a chance?</v>

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:54.750
<v David Whitfield>Um, I can't take that, sorry. I've only got the engineering notes, not the full shift handover.</v>

00:02:55.219 --> 00:03:02.569
<v Sarah Okafor>Okay, Cal, can you take that instead — send the shift handover report round this morning, whenever you get a chance?</v>

00:03:04.629 --> 00:03:09.879
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I'll send it round this morning. I've got the full report, so that's fine.</v>

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:16.680
<v David Whitfield>Cheers. Otherwise it'd be a very short report with most of the shift missing.</v>

00:03:18.289 --> 00:03:21.090
<v Aisha Begum>Some of us would appreciate a shorter report.</v>

00:03:23.379 --> 00:03:29.680
<v Callum Reid>Ha. On the other thing, I'll do a site visit at Tollgate with the contractor at half two.</v>

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:37.479
<v Sarah Okafor>Thanks, Cal. That one's if you've got a spare minute, rather than a priority over the production hold.</v>

00:03:38.699 --> 00:03:45.000
<v Callum Reid>Yeah, I've got room for it. I'll do Tollgate at half two with the contractor. Low priority, understood.</v>

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:49.650
<v Fiona Doyle>Half two, not twelve thirty? You clipped out a bit there.</v>

00:03:51.259 --> 00:03:55.110
<v Callum Reid>Half two. This headset's nearly as reliable as the weather forecast.</v>

00:03:56.250 --> 00:03:59.750
<v Marcus Hale>Leave the weather out of this, it's doing its best.</v>

00:04:00.819 --> 00:04:08.870
<v Sarah Okafor>Jamie, can you recalibrate the sensors on the GT2 inlet valve by the end of the week? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:04:10.870 --> 00:04:16.470
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, I'll recalibrate the sensors on the GT2 inlet valve by the end of the week.</v>

00:04:18.759 --> 00:04:23.310
<v Marcus Hale>Sorry, talked over you there — did you say end of the week?</v>

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:29.399
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, by the end of the week. Not treating it as an urgent one.</v>

00:04:29.990 --> 00:04:34.189
<v Sarah Okafor>That's right. It still matters, just not ahead of what's holding production.</v>

00:04:35.600 --> 00:04:44.699
<v Sarah Okafor>And I'll organise the toolbox talk for the team when I've got a spare minute. That's one for me, not another urgent job for everyone else.</v>

00:04:47.129 --> 00:04:49.579
<v Aisha Begum>Cheers, Saz. Toolbox talk's with you, then.</v>

00:04:50.100 --> 00:04:51.500
<v Sarah Okafor>Yep, I'll organise it.</v>

00:04:51.980 --> 00:04:57.930
<v Fiona Doyle>Sorry, was there a date on that? Or am I hearing the end-of-week bit from Jamie's job?</v>

00:05:00.250 --> 00:05:05.850
<v Sarah Okafor>No date for the toolbox talk. End of the week was the GT2 inlet valve sensors.</v>

00:05:07.930 --> 00:05:09.129
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, that's mine.</v>

00:05:10.720 --> 00:05:17.019
<v Aisha Begum>Okay. And the production hold is still the top one, rather than all of these being labelled urgent?</v>

00:05:18.209 --> 00:05:28.709
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. Fiona's permit to work and isolation for the Injection Moulding Line 1 needs doing first today. The others have the timings we've just agreed, but they're not all emergencies.</v>

00:05:30.899 --> 00:05:33.000
<v Fiona Doyle>Understood. That one's first for me.</v>

00:05:35.209 --> 00:05:39.759
<v Callum Reid>And handover's moved to me, not still sitting against David Whitfield as well.</v>

00:05:41.490 --> 00:05:47.790
<v Sarah Okafor>Yes, Cal, just you on sending the shift handover report round this morning. Whenever you get a chance.</v>

00:05:48.839 --> 00:05:51.290
<v David Whitfield>Lovely. No mystery duplicate version from me.</v>

00:05:52.360 --> 00:05:54.810
<v Marcus Hale>Two versions, both called final-final. Factory standard.</v>

00:05:57.000 --> 00:06:01.199
<v Sarah Okafor>Right, before we get onto file names — that's us. Thanks, everyone.</v>
